\b Keyboard Shortcuts for TY/TX/TU/TW\b0\par
\par
  \b File\b0\par
\par
    Ctrl+N                New file.\par
    Ctrl+F4               Close file, identical with Ctrl+N.\par
    Ctrl+O                Open file.\par
    F5                    Reload file.\par
    F8                    Recode file.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+F          Recode file as default encoding.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+A          Recode file as system default ANSI.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+O          Recode file as system default OEM.\par
    Shift+F8              Recode 7-bit ASCII file as UTF-8.\par
    Alt+F8                Reload file without file variable parsing.\par
    Ctrl+S                Save file.\par
    F6                    Save file as.\par
    Ctrl+F6               Save file copy.\par
    Ctrl+P                Print file.\par
    Alt+H                 Open recent file.\par
\par
  \b Tools\b0\par
\par
    Alt+N                 Open document in new window.\par
    Alt+0                 Open new empty window.\par
    Ctrl+M                Run metapath file browser plugin.\par
    Ctrl+L                Launch document.\par
    Alt+L                 Open with.\par
    Ctrl+R                Run command.\par
\par
  \b Favorites\b0\par
\par
    Alt+I                 Open favorites.\par
    Alt+K                 Add to favorites.\par
    Alt+F9                Manage favorites.\par
\par
  \b Edit\b0\par
\par
    Ctrl+Z                Undo.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Z          Redo.\par
    Alt+Backspace         Undo.\par
    Ctrl+Y                Redo.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Y          Undo.\par
    Ctrl+X                Cut.\par
    Shift+Del             Cut.\par
    Ctrl+C                Copy.\par
    Alt+C                 Copy all.\par
    Ctrl+E                Copy add.\par
    Ctrl+V                Paste.\par
    Shift+Ins             Paste.\par
    Ctrl+K                Swap.\par
    Del                   Clear.\par
    Ctrl+A                Select all.\par
    Alt+Shift+Arrows      Rectangular selection.\par
    Ctrl+Enter            New line with toggled auto indent option.\par
    Ctrl+PgUp/PgDn        Goto previous/next block.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+PgUp/PgDn  Select to previous/next block.\par
\par
  Char, Word\par
\par
    Ctrl+Space            Select word (or line).\par
    Ctrl+Backspace        Delete word before/left.\par
    Ctrl+Del              Delete word after/right.\par
    Ctrl+Tab              Insert tabulator.\par
\par
  Lines\par
\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Space      Select line.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Up         Move line (block) up.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Down       Move line (block) down.\par
    Ctrl+D                Duplicate line.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+X          Cut line.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+C          Copy line.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+D          Delete line.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Backspace  Delete line left.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Del        Delete line right.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+W          Column wrap.\par
    Ctrl+I                Split lines.\par
    Ctrl+J                Join lines.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+J          Join paragraphs.\par
\par
  Block\par
\par
    Tab                   Indent selected block.\par
    Shift+Tab             Unindent selected block.\par
    Alt+Q                 Enclose selection.\par
    Alt+D                 Duplicate selection.\par
    Alt+B                 Pad with spaces.\par
    Alt+Z                 Strip first character.\par
    Alt+U                 Strip last character.\par
    Alt+W                 Strip trailing blanks.\par
    Alt+P                 Compress whitespace.\par
    Alt+Y                 Merge blank lines.\par
    Alt+R                 Remove blank lines.\par
    Alt+M                 Modify lines.\par
    Alt+J                 Align lines.\par
    Alt+O                 Sort lines.\par
\par
  Convert\par
\par
    Ctrl+Shift+U          Make uppercase.\par
    Ctrl+U                Make lowercase.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+U            Invert case.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+I            Title case.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+O            Sentence case.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+S          Convert tabs to spaces.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+T          Convert spaces to tabs.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+S            Convert indenting tabs to spaces.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+T            Convert indenting spaces to tabs.\par
\par
  Insert\par
\par
    Alt+X                 HTML/XML tag.\par
    Ctrl+F8               Encoding identifier.\par
    Ctrl+F5               Time/date (short form).\par
    Ctrl+Shift+F5         Time/date (long form).\par
    Ctrl+F9               Filename.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+F9         Path and filename.\par
\par
  Special\par
\par
    Ctrl+Q                Block comment (toggle).\par
    Ctrl+Shift+Q          Stream comment.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+E          URL Encode.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+R          URL Decode.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+E            Escape C Special Chars.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+R            Unescape C Special Chars.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+X            Convert character to hex code.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+C            Convert hex code to character.\par
    Ctrl+B                Find matching brace.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+B          Select to matching brace.\par
    F2                    Expand selection to next match.\par
    Shift+F2              Expand selection to previous match.\par
    Ctrl+1                Enclose within ''.\par
    Ctrl+2                Enclose within "".\par
    Ctrl+3                Enclose within ().\par
    Ctrl+4                Enclose within [].\par
    Ctrl+5                Enclose within \{\}.\par
    Ctrl+6                Enclose within ``.\par
    Shift+F5              Update timestamps.\par
    Ctrl+Alt++            Increase number.\par
    Ctrl+Alt+-            Decrease number.\par
    Ctrl+,                Jump to selection start.\par
    Ctrl+.                Jump to selection end.\par
\par
  Find, Replace\par
\par
    Ctrl+F                Find.\par
    Alt+F3                Save find text.\par
    F3                    Find next.\par
    Shift+F3              Find previous.\par
    Ctrl+F3               Find next word or selection.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+F3         Find previous word or selection.\par
    Ctrl+H                Replace.\par
    F4                    Replace next.\par
    Ctrl+G                Jump to line.\par
\par
  Syntax scheme, Font\par
\par
    F12                   Select syntax scheme.\par
    Shift+F12             Select 2nd default syntax scheme.\par
    Ctrl+F12              Customize syntax schemes.\par
    Alt+F12               Select default font.\par
    F11                   Select default text syntax scheme.\par
    Ctrl+F11              Select web source code syntax scheme.\par
    Shift+F11             Select XML document syntax scheme.\par
\par
  View\par
\par
    Ctrl+W                Toggle word wrap.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+L          Show long line marker.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+G          Show indentation guides.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+N          Show line numbers.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+M          Show selection margin.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+8          Show whitespace.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+9          Show line endings.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+0          Show wrap symbols.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+V          Toggle visual brace matching.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+I          Highlight current line.\par
\par
  Zoom\par
\par
    Ctrl++                Zoom in.\par
    Ctrl+-                Zoom out.\par
    Ctrl+/                Reset zoom.\par
\par
  Settings\par
\par
    Ctrl+T                Tab settings.\par
    Alt++                 Increase limit for long lines.\par
    Alt+-                 Decrease limit for long lines.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+H          Toggle auto close HTML/XML.\par
    Alt+T                 Always on top.\par
    Ctrl+0                Transparent mode.\par
    Alt+F5                File change notification settings.\par
    Ctrl+9                Display text excerpt in title.\par
    F7                    Save settings now.\par
    Ctrl+F7               Jump to ini-file.\par
\par
  Misc.\par
\par
    Shift+F9              Copy pathname to clipboard.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+K          Copy window position to clipboard.\par
    Ctrl+Shift+P          Move window to default position.\par
    Esc                   Optionally minimize or exit \par
    Shift+Esc             Save file and exit \par
    F1                    Display version info.\par
\par
\par
Regular Expression Syntax\par
\par
  Note: the Scintilla source code editing component supports only a\par
  basic subset of regular expression syntax, and searches are limited\par
  to single lines.\par
\par
  .      Matches any character.\par
\par
  (...)  This marks a region for tagging a match.\par
\par
  \\n     Where n is 1 through 9 refers to the first through ninth\par
         tagged region when replacing. For example, if the search\par
         string was Fred([1-9])XXX and the replace string was Sam\\1YYY,\par
         when applied to Fred2XXX this would generate Sam2YYY.\par
\par
  \\<     This matches the start of a word.\par
\par
  \\>     This matches the end of a word.\par
\par
  \\x     This allows you to use a character x that would otherwise\par
         have a special meaning. For example, \\[ would be interpreted\par
         as [ and not as the start of a character set.\par
\par
  [...]  This indicates a set of characters, for example, [abc] means\par
         any of the characters a, b or c. You can also use ranges, for\par
         example [a-z] for any lower case character.\par
\par
  [^...] The complement of the characters in the set. For example,\par
         [^A-Za-z] means any character except an alphabetic character.\par
\par
  ^      This matches the start of a line (unless used inside a set,\par
         see above).\par
\par
  $      This matches the end of a line.\par
\par
  ?      This matches 0 or 1 times. For example, a?b matches ab and b.\par
\par
  *      This matches 0 or more times. For example, Sa*m matches Sm,\par
         Sam, Saam, Saaam and so on.\par
\par
  +      This matches 1 or more times. For example, Sa+m matches Sam,\par
         Saam, Saaam and so on.\par
\par
  *?     Causes * and + to behave non-greedy. For example, <.+> matches\par
  +?     all HTML tags on a line, whereas <.+?> matches only one tag.\par
\par
  \\d     Any decimal digit.\par
  \\D     Any character that is not a decimal digit.\par
\par
  \\s     Any whitespace character.\par
  \\S     Any character that is not a whitespace character.\par
\par
  \\w     Any "word" character.\par
  \\W     Any "non-word" character.\par
\par
  \\xHH   Character with hex code HH.\par
\par
  -----> Examples (don't use quotes)\par
         - Quote lines: find "^" replace with "> "\par
         - Unquote lines: find "^> " replace with ""\par
         - Remove line numbers: find "^[0-9]+" replace with ""\par
         - Convert tabs to double spaces: find "\\t" replace with "  "\par
         - Remove NULL bytes: find "\\x00" replace with ""\par
\par
